# Performance Evaluation Results

**Version:** 1.0.0
**Evaluation environment:** Okta developer sandbox (shared infrastructure)
**Test dataset:** synthetic_identities.json — 20 fictitious identities
**Runs per scenario:** 10

---

## Measurement method

Performance was measured using Workflows execution history timestamps in the Okta developer console. For each scenario, the elapsed time between the webhook receipt event and the key identity action defined as the SLA endpoint was recorded. This measures workflow-level latency only — the time from event receipt to the point at which the automation has completed its responsibility. It does not include downstream propagation time for SCIM-connected applications (which depends on Okta's provisioning scheduler) or manual task completion time (which depends on application owner response).

All ten executions per scenario were run sequentially using the same synthetic payload set. Timestamps were read directly from the Workflows execution history panel and recorded manually.

